            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>Data derived from weekly public opinion polls in the Netherlands in 1969 concerning social and political issues. Samples were drawn from the Dutch population aged 21 years and older.</p><p>All data from the surveys held between 1962 and 2000 are available in the DANS data collections.</p><p>Background variables:<br>Sex / age / religion / income / vote recall latest elections / party preference / level of education / union membership / professional status / < self > left-right rating / party alignment / province / degree of urbanization / weight factor.</p><p>Topical variables:<br>n6926: Whether there is prosperity, in general and in respondent's family.</p>"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
